{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788201964,"nonce":"/2CBx/ot0hn6jNzPDzpxEq67fsM=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCONFIRMED — this is the most accurate issue in the backlog on its source claims;\nevery hazard it names is real and I found no fabricated member. TWO CORRECTIONS,\nboth small in wording and one of which would have propagated a wrong sentence\ninto a source comment. And ONE ADDITION THAT SHRINKS THE WORK SUBSTANTIALLY.\n\n=====================================================================\nTHE ADDITION FIRST, BECAUSE IT CHANGES THE SIZE OF THE JOB\n=====================================================================\n\n**Participants, ordering and casualty chains need NO reflection at all. The\nacceptance's blanket \"built on field reads via a `BattleSafe`-style reflection\nlayer\" over-scopes the work by a large fraction.**\n\n`Verse/LogEntry` already exposes, public and abstract:\n\n    public abstract bool Concerns(Thing t);\n    public abstract IEnumerable\u003cThing\u003e GetConcerns();\n\nplus public `Tick`, `Timestamp`, `LogID`, `Age` and `def`.\n`BattleLogEntry_RangedImpact.GetConcerns()` yields `initiatorPawn`,\n`recipientPawn` and `originalTargetPawn`; `BattleLogEntry_DamageTaken.GetConcerns()`\nyields `initiatorPawn` and `recipientPawn`. Both are pure `yield return`\niterators — no writes, no Rand, no lazy init.\n\nAnd the containers are plain backing-list returns, not rebuilt caches:\n`Verse/Battle`: `public List\u003cLogEntry\u003e Entries =\u003e entries;`\n`Verse/BattleLog`: `public List\u003cBattle\u003e Battles =\u003e battles;`\n\nSo reflection is needed only for **weapon** (`weaponDef`/`projectileDef`),\n**body part** (`LogEntry_DamageResult.damagedParts` / `damagedPartsDestroyed` /\n`deflected`) and **attacker-vs-original-target disambiguation** — three fields,\nnot the whole surface. Worth restating in the spec, because \"a BattleSafe\nreflection layer\" reads as a large piece of infrastructure and most of what it\nwould wrap is already public.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 1 — \"EXACTLY ONE CALL SITE ... A MOUSE CLICK\". THE COUNT IS RIGHT;\n\"A MOUSE CLICK\" IS WRONG, AND THE ISSUE ASKS FOR THAT SENTENCE TO BE COPIED\nINTO A SOURCE COMMENT.\n=====================================================================\n\nThe call-site count is CONFIRMED: a full-tree grep for `Battle.GetName()` finds\nexactly one consumer, inside `RimWorld/ITab_Pawn_Log_Utility.GenerateLogLinesFor`\n(`tmpLogLines.Add(new LogLineDisplayableHeader(battle2.GetName()));`).\n\nBut its caller is `RimWorld/ITab_Pawn_Log.FillTab` — an IMGUI `FillTab`, i.e. it\nruns **every frame the Log tab is open**, not once per click. Ludeon gets away\nwith it for two reasons the issue does not name, and both are worth knowing\nbecause they are the reasons the pattern is safe for vanilla and unsafe for us:\n\n  (a) `FillTab` guards on a four-part cache key —\n      `if (cachedLogDisplay == null || cachedLogDisplayLastTick != selPawnForCombatInfo.records.LastBattleTick\n       || cachedLogPlayLastTick != Find.PlayLog.LastTick || cachedLogForPawn != selPawnForCombatInfo)`\n  (b) `Battle.GetName()` memoises into `battleName`, so the Rand burn happens\n      once per battle, ever.\n\nThe issue's acceptance says the forbidden list must name these methods \"and WHY\".\nAs drafted, the WHY contains this error and would be transcribed verbatim into\n`Source/AutoRimmer/`. Fix the sentence before it becomes a comment.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 2 — \"`LogEntry.def` IS NULL ON MOST ENTRIES\"\n=====================================================================\n\nDirectionally right, and the distribution is sharper than \"most\".\n`BattleLogEntry_MeleeCombat` is the ONLY entry whose constructor takes a\n`LogEntryDef def = null`, fed from `Verse/ManeuverDef.logEntryDef`, and ten core\nplus two Odyssey `ManeuverDef`s set it. `BattleLogEntry_RangedImpact`,\n`_RangedFire`, `_DamageTaken`, `_ExplosionImpact` and `_StateTransition` never\npass one. So it is **null on every ranged and damage-taken entry, and non-null on\nmost melee entries** — the ratio depends entirely on the melee/ranged mix, which\nis not a property of the game. \"Do not key anything on it\" is the right\nconclusion and should keep that reason rather than the frequency claim.\n\n(Related and CONFIRMED: only two `LogEntryDef`s exist game-wide, `MeleeAttack`\nand `SandInEyes`, in `Misc/LogEntryDefs/LogEntryDef.xml`, and\n`RimWorld/LogEntryDefOf` declares only `MeleeAttack`.)\n\n=====================================================================\nCONFIRMED, MEMBER BY MEMBER\n=====================================================================\n\n- `ITab_Pawn_Log_Utility`: `private static List\u003cLogLineDisplayable\u003e tmpLogLines`,\n  `GenerateLogLinesFor` opens `tmpLogLines.Clear();` and returns that same list.\n  CONFIRMED — and UNDERSTATED. `ITab_Pawn_Log.FillTab` stores that reference as\n  `cachedLogDisplay`, so an external call does not merely wipe the cache: it\n  REFILLS it with the other pawn's lines while `cachedLogDisplayLastTick`,\n  `cachedLogPlayLastTick` and `cachedLogForPawn` still report it fresh. The open\n  tab then renders the wrong pawn's log until an unrelated invalidation. Worse\n  than \"wipes\".\n- Same static-aliasing shape as `Verse/ListerThings.ThingsMatchingFilter`\n  (`private static readonly List\u003cThing\u003e tmpThingsMatchingFilter`, `Clear()` on\n  entry, returned). CONFIRMED.\n- `Verse/Battle.GetName()` lazy-inits `battleName` via\n  `GrammarResolver.Resolve(\"r_battlename\", request)`, and `Battle.ExposeData` does\n  `Scribe_Values.Look(ref battleName, \"battleName\");`. It has NO `Rand.PushState`,\n  and the resolver bottoms out in `RandomElementByWeightWithFallback` on the\n  shared stream. CONFIRMED on both counts — RNG burn AND scribed write.\n- `Verse/LogEntry.ToGameStringFromPOV` really does guard:\n  `Rand.PushState(); try { Rand.Seed = logID; ... } finally { Rand.PopState(); }`.\n  CONFIRMED, and the `finally` means it survives a throw.\n- It writes only unscribed instance caches (`cachedStringPov`, `cachedString`,\n  `cachedHeightWidth`, `cachedHeight`); `LogEntry.ExposeData` scribes only\n  `ticksAbs`, `logID`, `def`. CONFIRMED — with the consequence noted in the\n  acceptance section below.\n- The `PawnsFinder` chain is real end to end: `GrammarUtility.RulesForPawn` -\u003e\n  `PawnRelationUtility.TryAppendRelationsWithColonistsInfo` -\u003e\n  `GetMostImportantColonyRelative` -\u003e\n  `PawnsFinder.AllMapsCaravansAndTravellingTransporters_Alive_FreeColonistsAndPrisoners`,\n  whose body is `..._Result.Clear(); ..._Result.AddRange(...)`. CONFIRMED, and it\n  is exactly the Class E shape. `TryAppendRelationsWithColonistsInfo` also ends in\n  `.AdjustedFor(pawn, \"PAWN\", addRelationInfoSymbol: false)` — the nested grammar\n  resolve the issue names. CONFIRMED.\n- `Verse/ColoredText`: `private static Dictionary\u003cstring,string\u003e cache`, added to\n  in `Resolve`, cleared only by `ClearCache()` on a language/settings change. No\n  size bound. CONFIRMED unbounded. `RimWorld/GenLabel.labelDictionary` DOES have\n  a bound (`if (labelDictionary.Count \u003e 2000) { labelDictionary.Clear(); }`) —\n  and the issue correctly reserves the word \"unbounded\" for `ColoredText` alone.\n  Nice distinction; keep it.\n- The redundant unguarded push/pop: `PlayLogEntry_Interaction`,\n  `PlayLogEntry_InteractionSinglePawn` and `PlayLogEntry_InteractionWithMany` each\n  do `Rand.PushState(); Rand.Seed = logID; ... Rand.PopState();` with NO\n  try/finally, inside a base call that already pushed and already seeded.\n  CONFIRMED for all three. Net leak on a throw is one frame, since the base's\n  `finally` pops one of two.\n- `Verse/Root.Update` calls `Rand.EnsureStateStackEmpty()`, whose repair path is\n  `Log.Warning(\"Random state stack is not empty. ... Fixing.\")`. CONFIRMED — and\n  note it is a WARNING, which the journal records, so a leak is visible rather\n  than silent. Good news for the invariant.\n- No `BattleLogEntry_*` subclass adds its own push/pop; the only `PushState` in\n  that family is the guarded base. CONFIRMED.\n- `PlayLogEntry_InteractionSinglePawn : LogEntry` (not `: PlayLogEntry_Interaction`)\n  and re-declares its own `intDef`/`initiator`/`extraSentencePacks`/\n  `initiatorFaction`/`initiatorIdeo`. CONFIRMED — and note `PlayLogEntry_InteractionWithMany`\n  DOES inherit, so the trap is specific to `SinglePawn`.\n- The field inventory is accurate. `BattleLogEntry_RangedImpact` holds\n  `initiatorPawn`, `initiatorThing`, `recipientPawn`, `recipientThing`,\n  `originalTargetPawn`, `originalTargetThing`, `originalTargetMobile`,\n  `weaponDef`, `projectileDef`, `coverDef` — all private.\n  `BattleLogEntry_MeleeCombat` adds `implementType`, `ownerEquipmentDef`,\n  `ownerHediffDef`, `toolLabel`, plus two PUBLIC members: `alwaysShowInCompact`\n  and `RuleDef { get; set; }` — whose setter calls `ResetCache()`, so do not\n  touch it. Body parts live one level up in `Verse/LogEntry_DamageResult`\n  (`protected List\u003cBodyPartRecord\u003e damagedParts`, `damagedPartsDestroyed`,\n  `deflected`). CONFIRMED.\n- The fast path: `ITab_Pawn_Log.FillTab`'s guard is as quoted;\n  `Pawn_RecordsTracker.LastBattleTick =\u003e battleExitTick` is a bare field; and\n  `PlayLog.LastTick` is a count check plus `entries[0].Tick`. CONFIRMED.\n- `PawnSafe.Hidden(Pawn, Map)` exists and covers unspawned / wrong-map / fogged.\n  CONFIRMED.\n- Nothing named `combat-report`, `BattleSafe` or `BattleLog` exists in the repo\n  today. CONFIRMED — this is fully net-new.\n\n=====================================================================\nTHREE TRAPS IN THE FAST PATH THE ISSUE DOES NOT NAME\n=====================================================================\n\n1. **`LastBattleTick` is a FUTURE tick, not the tick of the last entry.**\n   `Pawn_RecordsTracker.EnterBattle` sets `battleExitTick = Find.TickManager.TicksGame + 5000;`.\n   It is a perfectly good monotone change TOKEN and a fatal thing to compare\n   against `TicksGame`.\n2. **`LastBattleTick` is PER-PAWN.** A colony-wide `combat-report` has no single\n   one. The colony-wide token must be constructed — max over pawns, or\n   `Find.BattleLog.Battles[0]`. The acceptance names `LastBattleTick` as though it\n   were global.\n3. **`Battle.LastEntryTimestamp` returns the OLDEST entry.** `Battle.Add` does\n   `entries.Insert(0, entry);` (newest first), and `LastEntryTimestamp` returns\n   `entries[entries.Count - 1].Timestamp`. Meanwhile `PlayLog.LastTick` uses\n   `entries[0]` and is correct. Do not assume the two containers agree on which\n   end is \"last\".\n\nTwo more write-on-read members in this neighbourhood, neither in the issue:\n`Verse/BattleLog.IsEntryActive` lazy-builds `cachedActiveEntries` — a HashSet of\nevery entry in every battle, on first read (unscribed, so benign for the save,\nbut not free). And `RimWorld/Pawn_RecordsTracker.BattleActive` walks\n`battleActive.AbsorbedBy` and ASSIGNS `battleActive` on read — and its\n`ExposeData` opens with `battleActive = BattleActive;` before scribing it, which\nis the write-on-SAVE class DESIGN's 2026-08-31 entry names. A per-pawn battle\nwalk must not touch `BattleActive`.\n\n=====================================================================\nACCEPTANCE — TESTABILITY\n=====================================================================\n\n- \"`GenerateLogLinesFor` and `ToGameStringFromPOV` named in its forbidden list and\n  WHY\" — testable by review; fix the WHY first (Correction 1).\n- \"participants, a per-pawn scoreboard, and a casualty chain naming attacker and\n  weapon\" — testable, and cheaper than the issue thinks (see the Addition).\n- \"Enemy participants fog-filtered per PawnSafe\" — **PARTLY UNTESTABLE, AND AS\n  WRITTEN IT HIDES THE REPORT'S OWN SUBJECT.** `PawnSafe.Hidden` returns true for\n  an unspawned pawn, and a battle-log entry routinely references pawns that are\n  dead, despawned or on another map — including the casualties the report exists\n  to describe. Applied literally, the rule erases them. The fog rule needs a\n  stated exception for pawns whose deaths are the report's content, or this\n  bullet passes by producing an empty report.\n- \"The `LastBattleTick` fast path demonstrated: two calls with no fight between\n  them, the second returning 'unchanged' without walking entries\" — the named\n  field cannot carry it (trap 2), and \"without walking entries\" is not observable\n  from the verb's JSON. Say how it will be observed (a counter in the result, or\n  DPA instrumentation) or the bullet cannot be failed.\n- \"a save-file diff showing the read wrote nothing\" — **testable, the right test,\n  and a PARTIAL detector that the issue should label as such.** It WILL catch\n  `Battle.GetName` (`battleName` is scribed) and `Pawn_RecordsTracker.BattleActive`\n  (scribed, and re-read during save). It will NOT catch\n  `LogEntry.ToGameStringFromPOV` (caches unscribed), nor `ColoredText.cache`, nor\n  `GenLabel.labelDictionary`, nor a Rand-stream burn. Necessary, not sufficient —\n  and the Rand burn is the one that matters most here, so pair it with a\n  `Rand.EnsureStateStackEmpty` warning check in the journal.\n- \"Zero red errors\" — testable on the bench.\n\n=====================================================================\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n=====================================================================\n\n- That the `ToGameStringFromPOV` cache fields never reach the save. I read\n  `LogEntry.ExposeData` and they are not in it; I did not diff a save.\n- The melee/ranged ratio behind Correction 2 — that is not a property of the\n  source at all, it is a property of a run.","files":null}]}